.TH BOSWAS-DOCUMENT-VIEWER 1 "November 2026" "boswas-apps 3.0~alpha1" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-document-viewer \- read, search and print PDF documents
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-document-viewer
.RB [ \-\-new\-window ]
.RI [ file " ...]"
.br
.B boswas-document-viewer
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-document-viewer
is Document Viewer, the PDF reader of Boswas OS. It is built on Qt PDF.
Each
.I file
opens in a tab. Only one instance runs per session: a later start hands its
files to the window that was active last and brings it forward, and a start
with
.B \-\-new\-window
opens a window of its own in the running instance (the desktop entry's
\(lqNew Window\(rq action, and the taskbar's \(lqNew window\(rq). The windows
share the list of recent documents.
.PP
The program runs as the desktop user and refuses to start as root. It only
reads documents; it cannot change them, and it has no annotation tools.
.SS Reading
Pages are shown in one continuous column, one page at a time, or two pages
side by side (optionally with the first page alone, as in a book). Zoom
goes from 10 % to 800 %, with fit to width, fit to page and actual size;
pages can be turned in quarter turns. The zoom box and the page box take
typed values; the page box understands the page labels of the document
(such as roman numerals) as well as plain numbers.
.PP
Pages are rendered on a separate thread at the resolution of the screen.
Only the pages on and near the screen are rendered and kept, within a
memory budget, so long documents scroll as easily as short ones. While a
sharper image is on its way the page is shown from the image it had before.
Above a size limit a page is rendered in parts: the part on screen at full
resolution over a coarser image of the whole page.
.PP
The sidebar shows page thumbnails, the outline (table of contents) of the
document, and the results of the last search.
.SS Searching
Search is incremental and runs on a thread of its own. It can match upper
and lower case exactly and whole words only. A query matches across line
breaks. All matches on the visible pages are marked, the current one in
another colour; the find bar counts them, and the Results tab of the
sidebar lists each with its page and the words around it. Going past the
last match continues at the first and says so.
.SS Text and links
With the text tool, dragging selects text on a page, a double click selects
a word and a triple click a line; the selection is copied with Ctrl+C. A
selection stays within one page. The hand tool drags the page instead.
The context menu copies, selects all text of the page, searches for the
selection and copies the page as a picture.
.PP
Links inside the document jump to their target; Back and Forward return.
A link to the web is never opened by the click alone: its address is shown
with an "Open link" button, and only that button hands it to the browser.
Only http, https and mailto addresses are opened.
.SS Protected, damaged and changed files
A document with a password shows a password page in its tab until the right
password is given. A file that is not a PDF document or is damaged shows an
error page. When an open file changes on disk, the application offers to
reload it and keeps the place in the document.
.SS Printing and presenting
Printing uses the system print dialog (printer, page range, copies, duplex
as the printer offers). Each page is rendered at the resolution of the
printer, scaled to fit the printable area and turned to match the paper;
a dialog shows the progress and can cancel. Printing needs the Qt print
support module (python3\-pyside6.qtprintsupport); without it there is no
Print command.
.PP
Presentation mode shows one page at a time on a black screen. Right, Down,
Space, Page Down, Enter or a click go on; Left, Up, Backspace, Page Up or a
right click go back; Home and End jump; Escape ends it.
.SS Keyboard
.TS
tab(|);
l l.
Ctrl+O|Open
Ctrl+S|Save a copy
Ctrl+P|Print
Ctrl+W|Close the tab
Ctrl+Tab, Ctrl+Shift+Tab|Next, previous tab
Arrow keys|Scroll
Page Down, Space|One screen down
Page Up, Shift+Space, Backspace|One screen up
Home, End|First, last page
Ctrl+G|Go to page
Alt+Left, Alt+Right|Back, forward
Ctrl++, Ctrl+\-, Ctrl+wheel, pinch|Zoom
Ctrl+0|Fit page
Ctrl+1|Actual size
Ctrl+2|Fit width
Ctrl+[, Ctrl+]|Rotate left, right
Ctrl+F|Find
F3, Shift+F3|Next, previous match
Ctrl+C|Copy the selection
Ctrl+A|Select all text of the page
F4|Sidebar
F11|Full screen
F5|Presentation
Alt+Enter|Document properties
Esc|Leave full screen, close the find bar, drop the selection
.TE
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-new\-window
Open the files in a new window, also when Document Viewer is already running.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.DocumentViewer/documents.json
Recent documents (at most 24) and the last page, zoom and page arrangement
of each document (at most 200).
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.DocumentViewer/window.ini
Size of the window.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/com.boswas.DocumentViewer/thumbnails/
Pictures of the first page of recent documents, for the start page.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/com.boswas.DocumentViewer.desktop
The desktop entry.
.SH SEE ALSO
